Sources for `compounding` skill (see plans/skill-audits/compounding.md for full audit):

- EveryInc/compound-engineering-plugin — https://github.com/EveryInc/compound-engineering-plugin — primary inspiration. The "compound engineering" principle from Every: each unit of work should make the next one easier.
- Conceptual lineage with two existing void-harness skills:
  - capture-rule — downstream destination for project-scoped patterns (writes .void/PROJECT-DOCTRINE.md under its own HITL gate).
  - harness-evolution — downstream destination for harness-scoped gaps (owns the feedback proposal format, the CLI, and the obsolescence audit).

Strategy: distill. Extract the "compounding work" principle and the end-of-cycle capture moment; rewrite as a routing ritual that feeds the two existing skills rather than a standalone capture mechanism.

What we reject (see audit note for rationale):
- The plugin's /ce-* command namespace — void-harness uses skill auto-discovery, not a bespoke command prefix.
- A per-cycle STRATEGY.md artifact — void-harness already routes lessons to PROJECT-DOCTRINE.md or harness-feedback; a third store would duplicate them and bloat the doctrine.

Design constraint: this skill writes NOTHING to doctrine itself. It names the pattern, decides scope, and routes. HITL lives in the destination skill.
